.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Minimal header-only unit-test framework for 42sh\&. 


.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
pulgamecanica (arosado-)
.RE
.PP
Provides shared pass/fail counters and assertion macros used across all test suites\&. No external libraries are required beyond libc\&.
.SS "Design"
!(assets/tests_meme\&.jpeg)[assets/tests_meme\&.jpeg]

.PP
\fRg_mu_passed\fP and \fRg_mu_failed\fP are declared \fRextern\fP here and defined exactly once in \fBtest_runner\&.c\fP so that every translation unit accumulates results into the same global totals\&.
.SS "Workflow"
Modules start life guarded by \fR#ifdef TEST_ (MODULE) _ENABLED\fP\&. Once an implementation is complete and all assertions pass the guards are removed and the corresponding \fR-D\fP flag is deleted from the Makefile\&. The test then compiles and runs unconditionally forever\&.
.SS "Quick-start — test file"
.PP
.nf
void test_something(void) {
    MU_ASSERT("truth holds", 1 == 1);
    MU_ASSERT_INT(42, compute_answer());
    MU_ASSERT_STR("label", "expected", get_string());
}
.fi
.PP
.SS "Quick-start — test_runner\&.c"
.PP
.nf
int main(void) {
    MU_RUN(test_something);
    MU_SUMMARY();
}
.fi
.PP
 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "static void mu_assert (const char * file, int line, const char * msg, int expr)\fR [inline]\fP, \fR [static]\fP"
Generic boolean assertion\&.

.PP
Evaluates \fIexpr\fP\&. Prints a green \fBPASS\fP line on success, or a red \fBFAIL\fP line including the source location on failure\&. Do not call directly — use the \fIMU_ASSERT\fP macro\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImsg\fP Human-readable description shown in the output line\&. 
.br
\fIexpr\fP Non-zero = pass, zero = fail\&.
.RE
.PP
Example:

.PP
.PP
.nf
MU_ASSERT("pointer is not null", ptr != NULL);
.fi
.PP
 
.SS "static void mu_assert_int (const char * file, int line, int expected, int actual)\fR [inline]\fP, \fR [static]\fP"
Integer equality assertion\&.

.PP
Compares \fIexpected\fP and \fIactual\fP as \fRint\fP values\&. On failure the output includes both the expected and the actual values\&. Do not call directly — use the \fIMU_ASSERT_INT\fP macro\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIexpected\fP The value the expression should produce\&. 
.br
\fIactual\fP The expression under test\&.
.RE
.PP
Example:

.PP
.PP
.nf
MU_ASSERT_INT(3, (int)ft_lstsize(list));
.fi
.PP
 
.SS "static void mu_assert_str (const char * file, int line, const char * msg, const char * expected, const char * actual)\fR [inline]\fP, \fR [static]\fP"
String equality assertion (NULL-safe)\&.

.PP
Compares \fIexpected\fP and \fIactual\fP with strcmp(3)\&. A NULL \fIactual\fP is treated as a failure and printed as \fR"(null)"\fP in the output line\&. Do not call directly — use the \fIMU_ASSERT_STR\fP macro\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImsg\fP Human-readable label shown in the output line\&. 
.br
\fIexpected\fP The expected C string (must not be NULL)\&. 
.br
\fIactual\fP The actual C string returned by the code under test\&.
.RE
.PP
Example:

.PP
.PP
.nf
MU_ASSERT_STR("newest entry", "pwd", history_prev(&h));
.fi
.PP
 
.SS "static void mu_run (const char * name, void(* fn )(void))\fR [inline]\fP, \fR [static]\fP"
Execute a test suite function and announce its name\&.

.PP
Prints a cyan header line with the name of \fIfn\fP then calls \fRfn()\fP\&. Typically used in \fRmain()\fP of \fBtest_runner\&.c\fP\&. Do not call directly — use the \fIMU_RUN\fP macro\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP Stringified name of the test suite function\&. 
.br
\fIfn\fP Function pointer to the test suite\&.
.RE
.PP
Example:

.PP
.PP
.nf
MU_RUN(test_list_suite);
.fi
.PP
 
.SS "static int mu_summary (void )\fR [inline]\fP, \fR [static]\fP"
Print the final pass/fail totals and return an exit code\&.

.PP
Must be called as the last statement in \fRmain()\fP via the \fIMU_SUMMARY\fP macro\&. Returns \fR0\fP if all tests passed or \fR1\fP if any test failed, so that \fRmake\fP can propagate the result\&.

.PP
Example:

.PP
.PP
.nf
int main(void) {
    MU_RUN(test_list_suite);
    MU_SUMMARY();
}
.fi
.PP
 
.SH "Variable Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int g_mu_failed\fR [extern]\fP"
Running total of assertions that failed\&.

.PP
A non-zero value causes MU_SUMMARY() to return exit code 1 so that \fRmake\fP can detect and report test failures\&. 
.SS "int g_mu_passed\fR [extern]\fP"
Running total of assertions that passed\&.

.PP
Defined in \fBtest_runner\&.c\fP; all test translation units share this counter through the \fRextern\fP declaration in this header\&. 
